# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret_key

# Data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
apps/api/data/

# A resume dropped in the repo root to try the importer on. Rooted, so the
# PDF fixtures the ingest tests read are still committed -- those are
# generated by scripts/make_ingest_fixtures.py and contain nobody's details.
/*.pdf

# Generated contracts are committed on purpose (they are the cross-language
# contract), but their build artifacts are not.
packages/contracts/.cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Impeccable working state. The direction contract (surfaces/), the build
# record (build/) and critique snapshots are history worth keeping; these two
# are not -- `questions/` is a decision-page server's scratch log, and
# `review/` is regenerable screenshot evidence, several hundred KB a round.
.impeccable/questions/
.impeccable/review/

# Notes, not the product.
#
# The design tool's own output, the architecture map, the product context and
# the decision records are all working material for whoever is building this.
# They stay on disk and out of the published repository. README.md is the
# exception: it is the repository's front page and belongs there.
.impeccable/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
*.md
# Anchored to the root: a bare `!README.md` un-ignores one at any depth, which
# let `models/README.md` back in.
!/README.md
